{"id": "DA-L04", "project": "Dashboarr", "round": "2026-11-07-bf3a060-review", "local_id": "L04", "title": "The Wake-on-LAN editor (and the service and header editors) accept values the import validator rejects, and nothing validates on export: one device with port 70000, 9.5 or -7 makes every backup of that config unrestorable with 'Config wolDevices entry is invalid'", "severity": "data-loss", "area": "front", "instincts": [6, 9, 27], "tags": ["latent"], "where": "app/(tabs)/(dashboard,services,settings)/wake-on-lan.tsx:80-92 (only name and MAC checked; port = Number(x) || 9), store/config-schema.ts:172-189 (coerceWolDevice: integer 1..65535, mac <= 32, broadcast <= 45, name <= 200), :613-622 (one bad entry throws for the whole import), store/config-store.ts:2764-2781 (export never runs validateExportPayload); same gap for the instance name (components/integrations/service-editor.tsx has no maxLength; coercer :76 caps 200) and header value/name lengths (custom-headers.tsx:28-41 checks only the name regex and CR/LF; coerceHeaderMap :62-67 caps 200/4096)", "smell": "Validation lives only at import time; the editors and the export path have looser or no limits (the coercer itself notes the class at config-schema.ts:118-119 for requestAsUserId)", "repro": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review/probes/probe_wol_import.js: 4 of 4 editor-accepted devices make validateExportPayload throw", "caught_by": "independent-review", "evidence": "reproduced", "status": "open", "origin": "pre-existing", "source": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review.md"}
{"id": "DA-L05", "project": "Dashboarr", "round": "2026-11-07-bf3a060-review", "local_id": "L05", "title": "A service URL stored without a scheme (older installs; the app normalizes it on read only) is exported as-is and rejected on import: the whole backup fails with 'Config services.<kind> entry is invalid'", "severity": "data-loss", "area": "front", "instincts": [6, 23, 27], "tags": ["latent"], "where": "store/config-store.ts:2615-2623 (getActiveUrl normalizes on read; comment says historical values lack http://), :3112 (export carries the stored value), store/config-schema.ts:41-50, :77-78 (isHttpUrlOrEmpty rejects '192.168.1.10:7878'), store/config-store.ts:824-834 (hydrate's isServiceInstance accepts any string)", "smell": "A value tolerated on every read path but rejected on one write path, with no one-time rewrite in storage", "repro": "reading: new URL('192.168.1.10:7878').protocol is '192.168.1.10:', so isHttpUrlOrEmpty returns false and coerceServiceInstance returns null", "caught_by": "independent-review", "evidence": "reading", "status": "open", "origin": "pre-existing", "source": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review.md"}
{"id": "DA-L06", "project": "Dashboarr", "round": "2026-11-07-bf3a060-review", "local_id": "L06", "title": "Removing a home network leaves every workspace that had selected it with only a dead id, which resolves to 'always remote' for good; re-adding the same WiFi gets a new id and does not repair it, though the import path repairs exactly this", "severity": "wrong-result", "area": "front", "instincts": [6, 56], "tags": ["latent"], "where": "store/config-store.ts:1945-1953 (removeHomeNetwork filters the global list only), :1918-1927 (addHomeNetwork mints a new id), lib/url-validation.ts:128-135 and lib/network.ts:77-88 (only-stale ids = forces remote), store/config-store.ts:2636-2637 (getActiveUrl returns remote, '' when none), lib/http-client.ts:544-546 ('No URL configured'), store/config-store.ts:700-712 (repairOrphanedHomeNetworkSelection runs on import only)", "smell": "A delete that removes a referenced row without pruning or repairing the references, while a sibling path (import) does repair them", "repro": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review/probes/probe_home_network_delete.js: remove Casa, add Casa -> workspace homeNetworkIds ['net-1'], effective [], forcesRemote=true; the import repair yields undefined/false", "caught_by": "independent-review", "evidence": "reproduced", "status": "open", "origin": "pre-existing", "source": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review.md"}
{"id": "DA-L07", "project": "Dashboarr", "round": "2026-11-07-bf3a060-review", "local_id": "L07", "title": "The Downloads widget's poster cache grows without bound in one AsyncStorage row (every downloadId ever seen in the queue or the last 50 history rows), and every storage write is fire-and-forget with no error handling; on Android a row past the 2 MB cursor window breaks initStorage and so hydrate, and a full store makes later saves fail silently", "severity": "crash", "area": "front", "instincts": [13, 25], "tags": ["latent"], "where": "hooks/use-torrent-poster-map.ts:22-44, :89-113 (additive, never evicted, persisted as one JSON value), store/storage.ts:7-13 (initStorage multiGet of every key), :21-24, :70-74 (AsyncStorage promises dropped, no catch)", "smell": "A 'sticky' cache keyed by an unbounded id space, persisted whole, with no cap or eviction; writes whose promise is never awaited", "repro": "reading only; the size at which it breaks was not measured (about 300 bytes per entry, so roughly 7,000 distinct downloads for 2 MB)", "caught_by": "independent-review", "evidence": "reading", "status": "open", "origin": "pre-existing", "source": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review.md"}
{"id": "DA-L08", "project": "Dashboarr", "round": "2026-11-07-bf3a060-review", "local_id": "L08", "title": "Importing a backup that carries no notificationSettings sets the store to defaults but leaves the previous device's settings in storage, so the notification toggles revert to the pre-import values on the next launch", "severity": "wrong-result", "area": "front", "instincts": [5, 6, 44], "tags": ["latent"], "where": "store/config-store.ts:2987-2992 (setJSON only if payload.notificationSettings), :3067 (store gets DEFAULT_NOTIFICATION_SETTINGS), :1415-1421 (hydrate reads the untouched key)", "smell": "A 'replace everything' import that writes a key conditionally while the in-memory state is set unconditionally", "repro": "reading: pre-import enabled=false persisted; import a v1-era backup; store shows enabled=true; relaunch shows enabled=false", "caught_by": "independent-review", "evidence": "reading", "status": "open", "origin": "pre-existing", "source": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review.md"}
{"id": "DA-L09", "project": "Dashboarr", "round": "2026-11-07-bf3a060-review", "local_id": "L09", "title": "The import wipes every current instance's SecureStore secrets and rewrites the per-kind service lists before the steps that can still fail (SecureStore writes, backend pair, Seerr drains); a failure there reports 'Invalid config file' while storage already holds the new config, the old secrets are gone and the running store still shows the old instances", "severity": "data-loss", "area": "front", "instincts": [8, 15], "tags": ["latent"], "where": "store/config-store.ts:2868-2873 (deleteSecret loop), :2883 (setJSON services), :2891-2899 (setSecret can throw), :2972-2982 (pair awaits SecureStore), :3029-3036 (drains), :3040 (set() only at the end), app/(tabs)/(dashboard,services,settings)/settings/backup.tsx:116-118", "smell": "Destructive writes before the last fallible step, with no rollback and no staging of the new values", "repro": "reading only; needs a SecureStore or pairing failure injected after line 2873", "caught_by": "independent-review", "evidence": "reading", "status": "open", "origin": "pre-existing", "source": "reviews/dashboarr/2026-11-07-bf3a060-review.md"}

